{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1461919-question-about-corpse-hide","id":1461919,"title":"Question about Corpse Hide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-28T22:51:08-07:00","id":1461919,"title":"Question about Corpse Hide","content":"Well the title is a bit misleading. However it was the thing that sent me down this rabbit hole in the first place.<br /> <br /> So the power let's the Fomori soak damage at 2 difficulty less. However, I use the combat rules in the VDA20 Companion which effectively makes it so players and SPCs don't need to roll. What can I do to compensate for this change, if anything?<br /> <br /> Corpse Hide is a power in the Book of the Wyrm on page 141.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":".  Made an error, and corrected it. 09-30-2021, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T04:00:54-07:00","id":1462111,"title":"","content":"For a Moment there I was psyched about a new combat system I didn't know, but page 345 of VDA20 describes pretty much the normal soak rolls. So, what rules are you talking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T10:52:01-07:00","id":1462139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1461919-question-about-corpse-hide?p=1462111#post1462111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a Moment there I was psyched about a new combat system I didn't know, but page 345 of VDA20 describes pretty much the normal soak rolls. So, what rules are you talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually very sorry. I meant the VDA20 Companion. At the end of the book it streamlines combat a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T15:37:07-07:00","id":1462329,"title":"","content":"Cool. Cool. Cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> In that case, the power should grant a bonus to the soak value (to be subtracted from damage), depending on the soak value one already has...<br /> <br /> If the soak was rolled, the average successes are nearing to be 50% more if the difficulty is reduced from 6 to 4, but only for really large dice pools. With small dice pools the effect isn't that large. So, I'd guess you get a bonus of 1 to your soak value, for a value of 3 and every increment of 3 thereafter. Adjust Hardening accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T16:12:03-07:00","id":1462342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1461919-question-about-corpse-hide?p=1462329#post1462329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool. Cool. Cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> In that case, the power should grant a bonus to the soak value (to be subtracted from damage), depending on the soak value one already has...<br /> <br /> If the soak was rolled, the average successes are nearing to be 50% more if the difficulty is reduced from 6 to 4, but only for really large dice pools. With small dice pools the effect isn't that large. So, I'd guess you get a bonus of 1 to your soak value, for a value of 3 and every increment of 3 thereafter. Adjust Hardening accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This actually helps me a bit, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}